          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the impact driver that fits your drill's batteries. For Milwaukee that is the M18 FUEL 2953-20, or the M12 FUEL 3453-20 for tight spaces; for DeWalt the DCF845 or the compact Atomic DCF850; for Ryobi the PBLID02, for Makita the XDT16, and for Bosch the GDR18V-1860CN.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ignore cross-brand torque comparisons, use impact-rated bits, keep the low mode for small screws, and let the drill handle the holes. Get those right and any driver on this list will make your next deck or cabinet job faster.
